TRHR treatment 24h- TaT1_24h_1X_100.1 JZ_24


TαT1 cells were maintained in monolayer culture on Matrigel-coated (Corning) vessels in DMEM media (high glucose, GlutaMAX™; Gibco) supplemented with 10% FBS (EURx) and 1% pen-strep. 
Cells were split 1:3 once they achieved 80% confluence. 
For thyrotropin releasing hormone (TRH, Sigma-Aldrich) stimulation experiments, the cells were plated at a density of 5,0 x 10^5 cells per well. 
For the stimulation, cells were maintained under DMEM medium (high glucose, GlutaMAX™) supplemented with 10% CS-FBS (Gibco), 1% penicillin-streptomycin and treated with 100 nM TRH and 60 mM KCl in singular pulse. 
Cells were cultured for 24h with the stimulant and harvested with Trizol for further RNA isolation. 
Stimulation experiments were based on Zatelli MC, et al., 2010)
